rows={
'routes':[
('Documented wages / current-account income','First choice if the funds are qualifying lawful income of an overseas individual. Buy FX and remit at a bank with identification and source documents, including tax documentation.','Direct, documented; the rule does not state a flat conversion tax.','Bank must verify the source; missing or unpaid tax documentation can delay processing. Actual tax and fees unknown.',W),
('Return unused foreign exchange','An overseas individual may remit unused foreign exchange received from abroad back through the original route with identification.','May avoid another RMB conversion if funds remain in foreign currency.','Does not establish a route for RMB already spent or other sources.',P),
('Reverse exchange of unused RMB','For RMB originally obtained by exchanging foreign currency, unused amounts may be converted back under specified receipt and identification rules.','Potentially useful for genuine leftover travel money.','Not a general route for wages; receipt and limits apply. Do not repeatedly split transactions to evade controls.',S),
('Foreign investment proceeds','Foreign-investment law implementation guidance lists capital contributions, profits, capital gains, asset-disposal earnings and liquidation proceeds as remittable in RMB or foreign currency.','Potential route for qualifying foreign investment.','Not a blanket personal-account exemption; ownership, investment registration, tax and bank review matter.',D),
('Inheritance / personal property transfer','The amended SAFE detailed rules identify outward transfer of domestic inheritance lawfully inherited by foreign citizens as governed by personal-property transfer rules.','Possible dedicated route for a genuine inheritance.','Applicability, documents, taxes and approval process need confirmation; not a general channel for wages.',S),
('Property sale proceeds','SAFE guidance discusses exchange and remittance of lawful domestic property transfer income of overseas individuals.','Possible source-specific bank route.','Requires verifying applicable current rules, ownership, sale and tax documents with bank; no rate established here.','https://www.safe.gov.cn/hebei/2019/0118/1253.html'),
('Overseas ATM withdrawal using a Chinese card','SAFE describes overseas cash withdrawals with domestic bank cards.','Useful for modest travel cash if the card and network work.','Cash rather than a US bank transfer; SAFE states annual RMB 100,000 per person and RMB 10,000 per card per day; bank fees and FX rates unknown.','https://www.safe.gov.cn/en/2017/1230/1391.html'),
('Spend overseas with a domestic card','SAFE distinguishes overseas card purchases from ATM withdrawals.','May pay genuine expenses directly.','Does not transfer a balance to a US account; merchant acceptance, limits and pricing vary.','https://www.safe.gov.cn/en/2017/1230/1391.html'),
('Carry RMB cash and exchange abroad','China’s government guide states a per-trip RMB cash carrying limit for visitors.','Can cover small legitimate travel needs.','The guide states RMB 20,000 per trip; US reporting and local exchange availability apply; theft and unfavorable spreads are risks.','https://english.www.gov.cn/2025special/bizexpatsinchina2025'),
('Payment institution for genuine transactions','SAFE rules describe licensed payment institutions handling certain cross-border transactions.','May be convenient where a supported legitimate transaction exists.','Source does not establish that an app can transfer this personal balance to a US account; eligibility and fees unverified.','https://www.safe.gov.cn/en/file/file/20190709/c4f05e09188549c4abf0c1a123441cc1.pdf'),
('Cross-border RMB then offshore conversion','Foreign-investment implementation guidance mentions remittance in RMB as well as foreign currency for qualifying foreign investors.','Allows comparison of onshore and offshore quotes if bank offers the permitted transaction.','Not verified for an ordinary personal savings transfer; receiving-bank acceptance, compliance and costs unknown.',D),
],
'costs':[
('Underlying China income tax','Depends on income type, tax residence, year, prior withholding and proof.','','China’s tax rules concern the income and filing facts; no account-specific liability can be calculated.','https://english.www.gov.cn/2025special/bizexpatsinchina2025'),
('Bank FX spread','Reference USD value − USD bought at the bank’s executable rate.','','Not an official tax. Compare quotes at the same time; reference rate and quote are unknown.',P),
('Transfer and intermediary charges','Sending fee + correspondent deductions + receiving fee.','','Ask for a written all-in quote and whether correspondent charges are deducted; actual charges unverified.',P),
('US income tax and relief','Worldwide income is generally taxable; foreign tax credit and earned-income exclusion have conditions and cannot both cover the same excluded income.','','Amount depends on the original income and filings, not simply where the balance sits.',I),
('Currency gain or loss','Currency movements can create US tax consequences in certain transactions.','','Basis, dates, transaction type and applicable exceptions are unknown; obtain tax advice.','https://www.irs.gov/pub/fatca/int_practice_units/limitation-exchange-gain-loss-debt.pdf'),
('Penalties and interest','Potential if tax or reporting obligations were missed.','','No default penalty or amount can be determined from the facts given.','https://www.irs.gov/businesses/small-businesses-self-employed/report-of-foreign-bank-and-financial-accounts-fbar'),
],
'compliance':[
('Foreign-account report (FBAR)','Generally file FinCEN 114 if aggregate foreign financial accounts exceed $10,000 at any time in the calendar year, subject to applicable rules.','Separate from income tax; file electronically.','https://www.irs.gov/businesses/small-businesses-self-employed/report-of-foreign-bank-and-financial-accounts-fbar'),
('Form 8938','Specified foreign financial assets may require Form 8938 if applicable thresholds are exceeded.','Thresholds vary by filing status and residence; separate from FBAR.',I),
('US worldwide income','US citizens generally report worldwide income regardless of residence.','Moving previously taxed principal is distinct from reporting underlying income; currency gains require separate review.','https://www.irs.gov/individuals/international-taxpayers/frequently-asked-questions-about-international-individual-tax-matters'),
('Foreign tax credit / earned-income exclusion','Foreign tax credits are subject to limits; qualifying earned income may be excluded under applicable conditions.','No credit for taxes allocable to excluded income. Compare outcomes with a qualified adviser.',I),
('Treaty','The US–China income tax treaty has a saving clause; some treaty provisions have exceptions.','Do not assume the treaty exempts a US citizen’s income.','https://www.irs.gov/pub/irs-trty/chintech.pdf'),
('US cash reporting','CBP requires reporting currency and monetary instruments over $10,000 in aggregate when entering the US.','FinCEN Form 105 is a reporting requirement, not itself a tax.',C),
('Avoid splitting and false documents','PBOC rules prohibit splitting to evade quota administration or using fabricated documentation.','Do not use friends’ quotas, sham gifts, or repeated transactions to circumvent controls.',P),
],
'flags':[
('Unknown origin and tax history','Whether this is salary, a gift, inheritance, property proceeds, an investment, or converted foreign funds is unknown.','No personalized optimal route or tax estimate can be verified.',P),
('Bank quotes / deductions','','Actual FX rate, spread, transfer fees, recipient charges and total net USD are unverified.',P),
('China and US tax amounts','','Income tax due, any penalties, foreign tax credits and currency gains are unverified.',I),
('Foreign individual classification','A US passport alone does not resolve all bank classification or tax-residence questions.','SAFE notes the annual facilitation quota applies to overseas individuals holding foreign permanent residence ID; do not assume a general $50,000 purchase allowance.',F),
('Repealed penalty provision','The amended SAFE detailed rules explicitly note that article 39 was repealed.','Do not rely on the outdated article 39 penalty figures; current penalty exposure is unverified.',S),
('Historical rules and changing practice','Several primary sources are historical and SAFE marks its detailed rules as amended.','Confirm current text and branch-level requirements before acting.',S),
('Property-sale classification','The 2019 SAFE FAQ calls property-transfer income current-account income; older PBOC text discusses approval for foreign individuals’ home-sale proceeds.','Potential overlap or subsequent policy change; ask bank/SAFE to confirm current procedure.','https://www.safe.gov.cn/hebei/2019/0118/1253.html'),
('Provider and offshore routes','','No official source here establishes eligibility for a generic personal wallet or offshore RMB transfer; do not treat either as a bypass.','https://www.safe.gov.cn/en/file/file/20190709/c4f05e09188549c4abf0c1a123441cc1.pdf'),
]}
labels={'index':'Overview','routes':'Transfer routes','costs':'Cost breakdown','compliance':'US & compliance','flags':'Flagged for review'}
intro={'routes':'Options depend on the legal source of funds. A payment method is not an exemption from exchange controls or tax.','costs':'There is no verified single “conversion penalty.” Separate tax already due from transaction costs and possible currency gains. Blank amounts mean unverified, not zero.','compliance':'Moving funds does not erase past filing obligations. US and China rules are separate; consult qualified cross-border professionals.','flags':'Open questions and source limitations are published here and do not imply a violation.'}
heads={'routes':['Route','How it works','Potential benefit','Limits / tradeoffs','Official source'],'costs':['Component','What it means','Verified amount','Caution','Official source'],'compliance':['Requirement','What official guidance says','Practical note','Official source'],'flags':['Issue','Known facts','Review required','Official source']}
def nav(active):
 return ''.join(f'<a class="{"active" if k==active else ""}" href="{k}.html" {"aria-current=page" if k==active else ""}>{v}</a>' for k,v in labels.items())
def table(name):
 result='<div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr>'+''.join('<th>'+escape(x)+'</th>' for x in heads[name])+'</tr></thead><tbody>'
 for row in rows[name]:
  result+='<tr>'+''.join('<td>'+escape(x)+'</td>' for x in row[:-1])+f'<td><a href="{escape(row[-1],quote=True)}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Official source ↗</a></td></tr>'
 return result+'</tbody></table></div>'
def shell(k,body):
 return f'''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><meta name="description" content="Evidence-led guide to moving funds from China to the United States."><title>{labels[k]} | China money guide</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="assets/style.css"></head><body><div class="layout"><aside><a class="brand" href="index.html"><span class="mark">↗</span><span>China money<small>RESEARCH GUIDE</small></span></a><p class="side-label">NAVIGATION</p><nav aria-label="Main navigation">{nav(k)}</nav><div class="side-note">Independent research<br><strong>Official sources only</strong></div></aside><main><header><span>RESEARCH / {labels[k].upper()}</span><span class="stamp">Reviewed 07 Nov 2026</span></header>{body}<footer>Educational information, not legal or tax advice. Rules and bank practice can change. <a href="flags.html">See research limitations →</a></footer></main></div></body></html>'''
home='''<section class="hero"><div class="eyebrow"><span></span> EXECUTIVE BRIEF</div><h1>Moving money from<br><em>China to the US.</em></h1><p class="lead">A practical, source-linked guide to understanding your options, costs, and obligations before moving funds across borders.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="routes.html">Explore transfer routes <span>↗</span></a><a class="text-link" href="flags.html">View open questions →</a></div></section><div class="stat-grid"><div><span>FIRST STEP</span><strong>Identify the source</strong><p>Salary, property, investment or previously exchanged funds follow different paths.</p></div><div><span>KEY DISTINCTION</span><strong>Tax ≠ FX cost</strong><p>Taxes, exchange spreads, bank charges and penalties are separate components.</p></div><div><span>STATUS</span><strong>Case-specific</strong><p>The amount, origin and tax history are unknown, so no net proceeds can be verified.</p></div></div><section class="summary"><div class="section-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">THE SHORT ANSWER</div><h2>Start with the paper trail.</h2></div><span class="number">01 / 04</span></div><p>If this is lawful salary or other qualifying current-account income of an overseas individual, the strongest first route to investigate is a direct bank conversion and wire using identity, source and tax documents. This is conditional—not a determination that the funds qualify or that no tax is owed.</p><p>A tax certificate may establish compliance with tax on the underlying income; it does not by itself prove a new tax is imposed on converting the balance. Compare the bank’s all-in USD proceeds, not just its quoted rate. <a href="https://www.safe.gov.cn/shanghai/2019/0215/988.html">SAFE salary guidance ↗</a></p><div class="callout"><strong>Do not assume the $50,000 allowance applies.</strong> SAFE distinguishes overseas individuals and identifies foreign permanent residence ID holders as eligible for annual purchase facilitation. <a href="https://www.safe.gov.cn/tianjin/2024/0621/2529.html">Read SAFE guidance ↗</a></div></section><section class="summary"><div class="section-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">YOUR RESEARCH MAP</div><h2>Explore the findings.</h2></div><span class="number">02 / 04</span></div><div class="cards"><a href="routes.html"><span>01</span><h3>Transfer routes ↗</h3><p>Compare documented pathways, benefits and constraints.</p></a><a href="costs.html"><span>02</span><h3>Cost breakdown ↗</h3><p>Separate transaction friction from actual tax liability.</p></a><a href="compliance.html"><span>03</span><h3>US & compliance ↗</h3><p>Review reporting, credits, and cash rules.</p></a><a href="flags.html"><span>04</span><h3>Flagged for review ↗</h3><p>See missing facts and unresolved eligibility.</p></a></div></section>'''
Path('index.html').write_text(shell('index',home))
for k in rows:
 body=f'<section class="page-title"><div class="eyebrow">RESEARCH LIBRARY</div><h1>{labels[k]}<em>.</em></h1><p class="lead">{intro[k]}</p></section>'
 if k=='costs': body+='<div class="callout"><strong>Comparison framework</strong> · Net USD = gross USD at executed rate − all transfer charges − any incremental taxes and penalties. A reference-rate comparison estimates FX spread; do not subtract it twice. Inputs are not available, so no numerical estimate is asserted.</div>'
 if k=='routes': body+='<p class="hint">Scroll horizontally on smaller screens to view the complete table. Source links describe the rule or transaction, not a guarantee of individual eligibility.</p>'
 body+=table(k)
 if k=='compliance': body+='<div class="callout"><strong>Next step:</strong> retain bank statements, records showing original source, tax filings and payment evidence, exchange receipts and remittance confirmations. Discuss missing filings with qualified advisers before moving funds.</div>'
 Path(k+'.html').write_text(shell(k,body))
